Skeleton Key 1.2.5
================================================================================
+ Optional "Bypass Multi-factor Authentication" setting to prevent the impersonated session from being redirected to Joomla's mandatory MFA setup page [gh-26]
+ Fresh installations of the package now enable its three plugins automatically (updates leave them as they are)
~ Plugins no longer load on PHP or Joomla versions outside the supported range, not just at install time
~ Funnelled the createQuery()/getQuery(true) compatibility branch through a per-plugin Helper\DbQuery::create() method
~ Raised the minimum requirement to PHP 8.1 and Joomla 5.4; dropped PHP 7.4-8.0 and Joomla 4.x support. Maximum supported versions are now enforced at install time (PHP 8.6, Joomla 6.2).
~ The key cookie now carries SameSite=Strict on Joomla 5 too; deprecated Joomla API usage removed
# [MEDIUM] An expired login key could still be used if removing expired keys from the database failed
# [MEDIUM] Impersonation could go unaudited if logging the request failed after the login key had been issued
# [MEDIUM] "Bypass Multi-factor Authentication = No" was ignored on sites with Joomla's default MFA options
# [MEDIUM] Skeleton Key did not work on sites using "Force HTTPS: Administrator only"
# [LOW] Login keys were issued for blocked users and users who must reset their password, who can never use them
# [LOW] Refused key requests and the use of a key were not recorded in the User Actions Log
# [LOW] A malformed Skeleton Key cookie caused a PHP warning
# [LOW] A copied login cookie presented from another browser could void the real user's key
# [LOW] Failed Skeleton Key logins were logged as "user 0" instead of naming the affected account
# [LOW] The anti-CSRF token and user ID of the login request were sent in the URL, ending up in access logs

Skeleton Key 1.2.4
================================================================================
~ Joomla 7 compatibility: plugins no longer rely on the removed automatic $app/$db population; application and database are injected through the service providers
~ Joomla 7 compatibility: the authentication plugin now uses SubscriberInterface and handles the AuthenticationEvent object directly (gated by Joomla version)
~ Joomla 7 compatibility: the onSkeletonKeyRequestLogin event now passes named arguments
  Minimum requirement raised to Joomla 4.4.

Skeleton Key 1.2.3
================================================================================
# [HIGH] Wouldn't work on Joomla 6 without the backwards compatibility plugin enabled

Skeleton Key 1.2.2
================================================================================
~ PHP 8.5 compatibility: setAccessible is deprecated for reflection objects
~ Joomla 5.4 and 6.0 compatibility: field UserGroupList renamed to usergrouplist (change of case)

